WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.871 --> 00:00:14.773
election will be next week?"

2
00:00:15.493 --> 00:00:17.014
Gliss blinked in surprise.

3
00:00:17.034 --> 00:00:19.997
"Laddno can't do that, can he?"

4
00:00:20.898 --> 00:00:23.119
"He did it," Fala said grimly.

5
00:00:23.139 --> 00:00:27.203
"Venna wants this to be over, so she didn't object.

6
00:00:27.703 --> 00:00:29.084
Neither did anyone else."

7
00:00:29.104 --> 00:00:31.606
"That makes sense," Darb said.

8
00:00:31.626 --> 00:00:36.914
"The longer the campaign goes on, the more time Laddno has to get people all riled up.

9
00:00:37.774 --> 00:00:40.696
So Venna probably wants the election as soon as possible."

10
00:00:40.716 --> 00:00:42.757
"I suppose you're right."

11
00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:44.298
Fala looked troubled.

12
00:00:44.318 --> 00:00:48.440
"It doesn't give us nearly as much time to stop Morb though."

13
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.641
"Yeah," Zann said.

14
00:00:50.661 --> 00:00:54.743
"Maybe we should try to rescue my parents before we go to the Far Frontier."

15
00:00:54.763 --> 00:00:56.945
"No," Perda said.

16
00:00:56.965 --> 00:01:02.708
"I'm sure Venna won't let anything bad happen to the prisoners, no matter what happens with the election."

17
00:01:03.524 --> 00:01:04.685
"But—" Zann began.

18
00:01:04.705 --> 00:01:07.708
"Think about it," Perda urged him.

19
00:01:07.728 --> 00:01:14.053
"Morb is a much bigger threat to everyone, including your parents, than anything that might happen with this

20
00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:16.935
election. We have to stop him."

21
00:01:17.756 --> 00:01:18.457
Darb nodded.

22
00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:22.680
"Besides, Wyssa won't wait for us if we try to rescue them.

23
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.223
For all we know, she already left for the Far Frontier."

24
00:01:26.243 --> 00:01:28.145
"I'll check."

25
00:01:28.905 --> 00:01:31.968
Fala hurried over and grabbed the Remote Eye from a shelf.

26
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.741
She put it to her eye.

27
00:01:33.761 --> 00:01:37.203
"Check the palace square," Perda suggested.

28
00:01:37.223 --> 00:01:39.385
"That's where we saw her last."

29
00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:40.846
Fala nodded.

30
00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:44.469
"I don't see her there," she reported after a moment.

31
00:01:44.489 --> 00:01:46.951
"I'm checking the streets nearby too."

32
00:01:48.011 --> 00:01:49.432
Zann was only half listening.

33
00:01:50.093 --> 00:01:52.435
He was still thinking about his parents and Boz.

34
00:01:53.095 --> 00:01:57.578
What if the election took place before Zann and the others returned from the Far Frontier?

35
00:01:58.179 --> 00:01:59.300
And what if Laddno won?

36
00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:03.334
Maff had told the kids that Laddno couldn't be trusted.

37
00:02:04.275 --> 00:02:06.376
What would he decide to do with the prisoners?

38
00:02:07.617 --> 00:02:09.398
Suddenly Zann had an idea.

39
00:02:09.418 --> 00:02:12.000
"Can you use that thing to look inside the palace?"

40
00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.201
he asked Fala.

41
00:02:13.881 --> 00:02:14.802
She lowered the Eye.

42
00:02:14.822 --> 00:02:16.503
"Sure," she said.

43
00:02:16.523 --> 00:02:21.446
"I've been checking on Venna whenever she's there, just in case something strange happens."

44
00:02:22.247 --> 00:02:23.087
"What about the dungeon?"

45
00:02:23.508 --> 00:02:24.128
Zann asked.

46
00:02:24.148 --> 00:02:25.789
"Oh, I see."

47
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:27.530
Fala scratched her chin.

48
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.552
"I'm not sure about that.

49
00:02:30.244 --> 00:02:33.006
There are probably spells protecting it from spies."

50
00:02:33.026 --> 00:02:35.027
"Can we try?"

51
00:02:35.387 --> 00:02:36.007
Zann asked.

52
00:02:36.027 --> 00:02:37.848
"I suppose it wouldn't hurt."

53
00:02:38.509 --> 00:02:39.990
Fala raised the Eye again.

54
00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:42.451
After a moment she smiled.

55
00:02:43.291 --> 00:02:44.472
"Hey, it does work!

56
00:02:45.052 --> 00:02:46.293
I can see everyone.

57
00:02:46.593 --> 00:02:47.854
They all look fine."

58
00:02:48.474 --> 00:02:49.615
She gestured to Zann.

59
00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:50.776
"Take a look."

60
00:02:51.416 --> 00:02:53.497
Zann eagerly peered into the Eye.

61
00:02:54.158 --> 00:02:57.900
He gasped as he saw his parents, Boz, Teplo, and the others.

62
00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:01.061
They were talking quietly to one another from their cells.

63
00:03:02.302 --> 00:03:07.864
"I can't believe there are no Shield spells on the dungeon," Gliss said, reaching for the Eye.

64
00:03:07.884 --> 00:03:09.505
"Can I check on my uncle?"

65
00:03:09.525 --> 00:03:12.686
"There probably are spells," Perda said.

66
00:03:12.706 --> 00:03:16.488
"But the Remote Eye is a very old form of magic, remember?

67
00:03:17.308 --> 00:03:19.809
Maybe the spells don't protect against stuff like that."

68
00:03:19.829 --> 00:03:22.931
"That's probably the case," Fala agreed.

69
00:03:22.951 --> 00:03:25.868
"Now let's see if we can locate Wyssa."

70
00:03:25.888 --> 00:03:28.510
The kids took turns scanning the city with the Eye.

71
00:03:29.271 --> 00:03:34.675
Meanwhile Fala tried a few other Search spells, but nothing worked.

72
00:03:34.695 --> 00:03:38.819
"Maybe she really did leave without us," Gliss said.

73
00:03:38.839 --> 00:03:41.281
"Now what are we going to do?"

74
00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:42.542
Perda exclaimed.

75
00:03:42.562 --> 00:03:45.945
"I know one place we haven't checked," Darb said.

76
00:03:46.545 --> 00:03:49.908
Zann glanced at his friend, who was scratching Zing with one hand.

77
00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:56.098
The sniffer goose was cuddled up against Darb's other side, honking softly as she drifted off to sleep.

78
00:03:56.118 --> 00:03:58.738
"Where?" Fala asked.

79
00:03:58.758 --> 00:04:00.999
"The zoo," Darb replied.

80
00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:03.440
"That's where she took us before, remember?"

81
00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:04.800
"Let me check."

82
00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.761
Fala raised the Remote Eye to her face.

83
00:04:08.401 --> 00:04:10.262
As soon as she looked through it, she gasped.

84
00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:13.383
"There she is—in a dragon pen!

85
00:04:14.103 --> 00:04:15.263
But what's she doing?"

86
00:04:16.924 --> 00:04:17.844
Perda grabbed the Eye.

87
00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:22.062
"It looks like she's cleaning up dragon scales," she reported.

88
00:04:22.082 --> 00:04:24.043
"That's weird."

89
00:04:25.424 --> 00:04:30.167
"Not if she needs the scales for some kind of travel spell," Fala pointed out.

90
00:04:30.187 --> 00:04:31.508
"We'd better hurry.

91
00:04:32.128 --> 00:04:34.209
She could decide to leave at any moment."

92
00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.231
"We?" Zann glanced at Fala.

93
00:04:37.251 --> 00:04:38.432
"Are you coming with us?"

94
00:04:39.292 --> 00:04:39.833
She shrugged.

95
00:04:39.853 --> 00:04:42.254
"I'd love to see the Far Frontier."

96
00:04:42.274 --> 00:04:44.215
"But what about the animals?"

97
00:04:44.675 --> 00:04:45.276
Darb asked.

98
00:04:46.356 --> 00:04:50.558
"I thought you might want to stay with them this time," Fala told Darb, smiling.

99
00:04:50.578 --> 00:04:52.799
"No!" Zann blurted out.

100
00:04:52.819 --> 00:04:55.080
"We can't leave Darb behind."

101
00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.241
"But he's so good with animals," Fala said.

102
00:04:58.261 --> 00:05:00.962
"This is where he can be most helpful."

103
00:05:01.622 --> 00:05:02.683
Gliss shook her head.

104
00:05:02.703 --> 00:05:06.404
"He's most helpful with us," she said firmly.

105
00:05:06.424 --> 00:05:08.985
"That's right," Perda agreed.

106
00:05:09.405 --> 00:05:13.347
"I've lost count of how many times Darb has helped us during our travels."

107
00:05:14.668 --> 00:05:15.368
Zann nodded.

108
00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.681
"He might not have magic, but he has skills the rest of us don't have."

109
00:05:20.541 --> 00:05:24.582
Fala looked surprised, but she raised both hands in a gesture of surrender.

110
00:05:24.602 --> 00:05:27.063
"All right," she said with a smile.

111
00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:28.964
"You've convinced me.

112
00:05:29.624 --> 00:05:31.844
Darb can go with you, and I'll stay here.

113
00:05:32.445 --> 00:05:34.225
But be careful, all right?"

114
00:05:35.005 --> 00:05:38.446
"We will," Zann promised, reaching for his friends' hands.

115
00:05:38.466 --> 00:05:44.948
"Zap!" They landed in a little fountain filled with moon minnows and other fish.

116
00:05:45.904 --> 00:05:49.006
"Ugh, what is it with you and water, Zann?"

117
00:05:49.327 --> 00:05:50.067
Gliss complained.

118
00:05:50.768 --> 00:05:53.690
She climbed out and used magic to dry herself and Darb.

119
00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.351
"Never mind that."

120
00:05:55.911 --> 00:05:57.873
Zann jumped out of the fountain and looked around.

121
00:05:57.893 --> 00:06:00.755
"Which dragon pen was Wyssa in when you saw her?"

122
00:06:00.775 --> 00:06:04.878
"It wasn't the big one with the mean dragons," Perda said.

123
00:06:04.898 --> 00:06:08.400
"I think I saw a cloud glider in the background."

124
00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:10.722
"That pen is this way."

125
00:06:11.443 --> 00:06:16.569
Darb led the way along a path and around a large display of animals native to the Magica

126
00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:21.731
Mountains. When they rounded the corner, Wyssa was just letting herself out of the dragon pen.

127
00:06:22.392 --> 00:06:24.132
She frowned when she spotted the kids.

128
00:06:24.152 --> 00:06:27.734
"It's about time you got here," she snapped.

129
00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:32.375
"I hope you're ready, because we're leaving for the Far Frontier right now."
